  "2026-11-11T08:54:52.636Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Read issue 339 and queue rules. Classify section-local reorder first, exact previous-renderer equality second, remaining drift as tracker_changed. Store rendering versions in the JSON receipt without changing Markdown bytes. Audit all four prior in_progress items against merged commits and release tags; close delivered historical items as explicitly requested, keeping this issue in_progress."
  "2026-11-11T09:01:06.423Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Tracker audit complete: pmc-total-item-order delivered by #324 in v2026.11.7; pmc-stable-itemless-check by #333 and pmc-contract-changes by #328 in v2026.11.10. Closed those with actual merge timestamps and release evidence. Also closed pmc-no-empty-unreleased-337 as merged via #338 but not yet tagged. No other prior in_progress items remain. Operator facet on pmc-total-item-order supplies the 2026.11.7 regeneration action through the existing native catalog. The pinned CLI required activating the local package field registration before writing change_facets; used an ignored local extension installation."
  "2026-11-11T09:12:34.082Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Current regression suite passes 9/9 in the disposable revert harness before and after four independent behavioral mutations. Reverting only main diagnostics fails both reorder and new-item tests (2/2 failures); changing only the check failure exit to zero fails both exit assertions (2/2); removing only the previous rendering profile fails its test (1/1); removing only the catalog facet with pinned pm fails the upgrade action test (1/1). All failures are assertions, not setup or syntax errors. Source worktree was never mutated. Typecheck and test typecheck pass; docstring gate covers 281 declarations in 52 files. No lint script is configured. Registered host checks now share the diagnosis and preserve typed exit-1 errors. Starting the full npm suite within the 45-minute gate cap; CI retains responsibility for full release coverage and Bun release gates under this task budget."
  "2026-11-11T09:13:25.759Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Regeneration initially dropped existing dependency-only notes when the corrected releases acquired closed items: default dependency fallback applies only to itemless windows. Enable the existing --dependency-updates option in this package full-changelog script so the historical dependency notes remain alongside the newly attributed delivered items. No generator default or dependency pin changes."
  "2026-11-11T09:49:31.319Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Full npm test passed 1072/1072 across 50 suites with zero failures, skips or cancellations in 1616 seconds. The longest lifecycle test took 1095.6 seconds, within the requested 20-minute file budget. Trailing npm flags were ignored by Node, so this run supplies no coverage evidence. Subsequent review found and fixed the previous revision dependency-selection path: the same rendering revision now flows through selection, immutable tagged heading detection and merging. The added real tracker/Git snapshot regression passes, becomes tracker_changed after a genuine new item, and fails when only the previous heading rule is reverted. Updated disposable proof: 10/10 fixed, five behavioral mutations causing seven assertion failures, then 10/10 restored. Final focused validation puts all flags before test paths and covers 40 affected files with a separate 100-percent classifier-module coverage threshold. Final-head full release and Bun gates remain CI responsibilities under the task budget."
  "2026-11-11T10:02:01.207Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final focused gate PASS: 871/871 tests across 37 suites in 40 files, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 788.35 seconds. Correctly ordered native coverage reports 100 percent lines, branches and functions for src/check-drift.ts only; no all-source or statement coverage claim. Every direct importer of changed modules was exercised in the earlier 1072-test full suite, including the 18-minute lifecycle stress file. Final-head full-suite/release/Bun certification remains with CI. Confirmed origin/main is still the branch starting head f231c38. Programmatic native-host regeneration fallback also retains the authoritative tracker path; transport regressions are rerunning before commit."
  "2026-11-11T10:05:52.080Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final transport gate passes 31/31 (the ten new regressions plus registered extension tests), with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate pass again (281 declarations, 52 files); no lint script exists. The latest pinned pm test --run --match prove-check-generator-drift-revert.ts --progress passes in 47.5 seconds: fixed 10/10, five independent mutations producing seven assertion failures, restored 10/10. All behavioral mutation work remains in disposable copies. The CLI refused editing a linked test command identity as designed; atomically replaced the entry through its prescribed remove/add recovery and linked the exact successful focused and transport commands. No pm CLI/SDK defect or out-of-scope code blocker was found. Keep this item in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-11T10:09:51.128Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/341 with implementation commit b34a05c. Local evidence: full npm 1072/1072 before the final selection edge case; final affected suites 871/871 across 40 files with classifier-only 100-percent lines/branches/functions; final transport 31/31; pinned behavioral proof fixed 10/10, five mutations causing seven assertion failures, restored 10/10. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, docstrings and changelog/link check passed. No lint script is configured. Full final-head release coverage, full-suite CI and Bun gates are pending and are not claimed as approval. Releasing this own claim for orchestrator verification; the item remains in_progress. The final receipt commit will preserve all historical audit prefixes and rerun the changelog after these tracker writes."
  "2026-11-11T11:53:34.227Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Resumed the scoped review round at 643e0e1 with a clean worktree. Read all nine unresolved threads and all nine full comments/diff hunks, with pagination complete. Classes: parsed-model regeneration commands including canonical host flags, stdin and cross-platform quoting; rendering-version evidence plus complete multiline entry blocks; native upgrade declarations for the two 2026.11.10 rendering changes; portable behavioral proof baselines. Preserve the accepted classifier architecture, append-only tracker history, and prior gate evidence. Do not reply to or resolve review threads; provide the per-thread fix table for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-11T12:26:22.032Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Review classes A-D implemented. Parsed-model commands keep canonical flags and equals-form pm-arg pairs, ignore embedding argv, retain the native tracker path once, provide PowerShell plus lossless argv, and require the original stdin pipe without advertising a standalone command. Upgrade attribution requires an exact previous-renderer match AND different declared revisions; unproved/current-version reorders explain timestamp or manual edits. Blank-separated details remain entry units. Added distinct 2026.11.10 contract and empty-pending upgrade facets and a rendering-change tag/catalog invariant. Proof baseline chooses a pinned merge base or working-tree source and owns its diagnostic mutation, avoiding no-op fallback. Initial gates: 16/16 regression tests, classifier-only 100 percent lines/branches/functions, 3/3 baseline selection controls; 15 independent behavioral mutants caused 17 assertion failures followed by 16/16 restored controls. Both requested B regressions fail on their function-only mutations. Full source-clone/archive proof and all importing test files are next; prior completed delivery hygiene is preserved."
  "2026-11-11T13:17:04.718Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Scoped review round PASS: complete npm-test-equivalent build/build:test and all 57 test files ran with flags before paths, two workers, per-file 1200-second timeout and overall 2700-second cap. Result 1083/1083 across 50 suites, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 1963.27 seconds; the longest lifecycle case was 1177.06 seconds. New focused regressions pass 16/16; classifier-only coverage is 100 percent lines/branches/functions. Portability gate passes 4/4, executing the complete proof in a fresh single-branch clone and a source archive; those also pass within the full run. Refreshed three baseline controls verify the additional ancestor-checkout and inherited-Git-context guard. Latest pinned pm proof run passed 16 controls, 15 independent mutations with 17 expected assertion failures, and 16 restored controls. Both B function-level reverts fail their new regressions; A command/pipe/Windows/alias, both C catalog actions, and D baseline prerequisite each have mutation evidence. The new copy/run fixture initially exposed a missing manifest in the disposable package; copied that manifest and the final runs pass. No pm CLI/SDK defect was found. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, and docstrings pass (283 declarations, 53 files); no lint script exists. Win32 quoting/argv is unit-tested; actual copied commands were executed on POSIX and the native pm host, with no live Windows claim. All nine full comments and diff hunks were read with complete pagination; no thread replies or resolutions were sent."
