  "2026-11-11T22:27:34.455Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round 5: worktree is clean at accepted head 547eb81; fetched origin/main and it remains merged 9b2c446, so no new merge is needed. Read all three new review threads in full, including every comment and diff hunk with complete pagination: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62YOap (release recovery freeze), PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62X8GM (historical contract formatting), PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62YOau (matched-profile wording). Preserve accepted rounds. Implement a proven release preparation/tag commit boundary for attribution, skip/log unproved or later completions, retain each old profile contract formatting, and avoid asserting an inferred committed generator version. Real native tracker recovery/must-allow tests and behavioral reverts will precede bounded gates."
  "2026-11-11T22:46:48.546Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Focused round-5 checks pass: 24 drift tests and four release-attribution tests. Registry absence explicitly permits an unpublished preparation window; published or unknown versions cannot use a later recovery HEAD as a fresh window. Read-only Git resolves the original preparation/tag boundary and reads native item snapshots through the public SDK reader. Eligible items must be closed in that snapshot, carry the same explicit completion before the commit time, and retain the same rendering declaration; otherwise log and leave unattributed. Late and backdated-new items remain Unreleased and the published release section is byte-identical. Non-git/unproved publication cases skip with item logs. Historical profiles now retain ordinary contract grouping, entry-from prose and breaking-entry behavior, verified against text goldens captured from the published npm 2026.11.6 CLI. Messages describe matched profiles rather than asserting producer versions."
  "2026-11-11T23:05:51.429Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final round-5 drift proof PASS in 180.08 seconds: 24 fixed controls, 44 independent mutations causing 46 expected assertion failures, 24 restored controls; all 46 proof cases reported successfully. New reverts cover published recovery cutoff (including backdated-new items), unpublished draft must-allow, unknown publication refusal, canonical exact-version registry lookup, workflow base-SHA wiring, legacy profile formatting and five formatting/grouping functions independently, and matched-profile wording in CLI/extension. Five attribution regressions pass on real native trackers/Git snapshots and a real local HTTP registry fixture; no SDK mocks. The gate dependency graph plus CLI/worker and workflow-data readers selects 51 test files. Each is running in its own timeout-1200 process with no more than two workers, isolated HOME/Git configuration and credential-free npm settings. Code is frozen during these gates; all exact per-file commands are linked as tests."
  "2026-11-11T23:17:43.717Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Bounded gate update: test/release-lifecycles.test.ts timed out at 1200.05 seconds with exit 124; no assertion failure appeared before the cap, and its first case passed. The native 500-lifecycle case is incomplete and is not claimed as passed. Evidence added to existing pmc-lifecycle-test-budget (no duplicate follow-up created). All other completed file gates have passed so far; remaining gates continue. Keep requested 20-minute limits and stress scale unchanged, and report this explicit local validation gap alongside final results and current-head CI status."
  "2026-11-11T23:28:31.415Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round-5 final bounded importer/workflow gate finished: 51 files attempted with strict 1200-second per-file wrappers, at most two workers, isolated HOME/Git configuration and credential-free npm settings. Fifty files passed: 1013 reported tests across 47 suites, zero assertion failures/skips/cancellations in completed files. One file is incomplete: test/release-lifecycles.test.ts hit the cap at 1200.05 seconds (exit 124); first case passed, native 500-lifecycle case unfinished, no assertion failure before termination. Existing pmc-lifecycle-test-budget holds the receipt; no limits or stress scale were weakened. Overall gate wall time was 1663.65 seconds. Complete fresh-clone/source-archive proof passed within its 571.89-second file gate. Pinned normal proof passes 24 fixed controls, 44 mutations with 46 expected assertion failures, 24 restored controls; all 46 cases reported. Focused 24 drift and five attribution/registry tests pass. Typecheck, build, test compilation, docstrings (57 files, 289 declarations) and publish-attestation audit pass; no lint script is configured. The existing lifecycle budget gap and full release certification remain with exact-head CI; do not present the entire local gate as green."
  "2026-11-11T23:28:32.531Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round-5 handoff mapping: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62YOap uses the decision base, registry publication evidence and original Git/native snapshot cutoff; published recovery cannot stamp later or backdated-new items, an unpublished draft permits its own proven window, and unproved candidates are logged. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62X8GM retains each profile contract grouping/entry/close-reason/breaking formatting, verified against published npm 2026.11.6 text goldens. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62YOau says matches rendering profile in CLI and extension while retaining compared_rendering_version. Three complete threads/comments/diff hunks read with complete pagination; no replies or resolutions. Main remained merged 9b2c446; accepted history is preserved. Commit source/dist/docs/tests and native pm evidence together, release only this own claim while keeping the own item in_progress, regenerate/check changelog after final writes and push the same PR. Lifecycle-budget follow-up remains open and its ownership is unchanged."
  "2026-11-11T23:56:05.565Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round 6: read all four CodeRabbit threads and AI-agent prompts completely (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CP, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CM, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CT, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CE). Accepted head 8dcf593 preserved; fetched main 9b2c446 is already merged. Plan: use only reachable published gitHead or tag for published snapshots, reject frozen non-change closures and inconsistent delivery facts, make command assertions/execution shell-aware, and document the two file-check receipt classifications. Add real-tracker allow/refuse cases and disposable behavioral reverts; run requested bounded importer gates, excluding lifecycle stress locally as instructed. Never close the own item or answer/resolve review threads."
  "2026-11-12T00:05:18.181Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round-6 implementation complete: published attribution uses npm gitHead (tag only if absent), verifies its package version and ancestry from fetched main, and never substitutes the first version commit or recovery base. Missing/invalid/unknown publication evidence produces per-candidate reason codes and no stamps; proven unpublished windows retain must-allow behavior. Frozen done status, explicit non-change dispositions, normalized status, completion timestamps and rendering declarations all gate native attribution. Real tracker coverage includes F-before-P publication, post-P refusal, stale tag versus gitHead, missing main, wrong/unreachable objects, relabelled duplicate/not-planned closures, active/canceled snapshot rows, corrected timestamps and changed facets/contracts. Shell tests validate with the existing regeneration helper, route execution explicitly to sh or PowerShell, preserve quoted values in Windows-compatible filenames, and exercise both interpreter choices without claiming live Windows execution. Usage now documents only rendering_changed/tracker_changed file receipts. pm test --run --match test/rendering-release-boundary.test.ts --progress passed the six boundary tests. Scoped gates include all script importers, the proof consumer and shipped-document checks; lifecycle stress is explicitly excluded locally as requested."
  "2026-11-12T00:11:43.828Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round-6 revert evidence: shared disposable proof passed all 56 cases: 25 fixed controls, 54 independent behavior mutations producing 56 expected assertion failures, then 25 restored controls. Added mutations cover first-version versus actual publication, forbidden recovery-base advance, stale-tag override, main reachability, frozen non-change/time/facets, POSIX-only assertion/default-shell regression, and file-receipt documentation. An additional disposable full-function proof restored the accepted round-5 boundary module alone: both the intervening-item must-allow and post-publication must-refuse tests fail as assertions (2/2). Restoring only the round-5 attribution module fails frozen non-change delivery (1/1); restoring old usage docs fails its contract test (1/1); reinstating the original POSIX-only assertion fails the PowerShell fixture (1/1). Fourteen fixed controls pass before and after all four independent reverts; source worktree never mutated. All expected failures are assertions, not setup/syntax/timeouts. Focused new boundary 6/6, attribution/registry 6/6 and check-generator-drift 25/25 pass; final bounded importer/document gates are running with lifecycle stress excluded."
  "2026-11-12T00:16:00.483Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final portability audit found three fixture-only --pm-bin overrides pointing at the POSIX npm shim. Removed those overrides so the genuine CLI tests use the existing production resolver (Node plus the installed package manifest), including on Windows. Explicit copied-command execution still uses the shell the guidance reports; the registered host command uses PowerShell's npm shim discovery on Windows. No production module changed after the prior behavior proofs. Repeat only the affected check-generator-drift and fresh-clone/source-archive proof gates on the final fixture text; all other completed scope results remain applicable. Lifecycle stress remains excluded."
  "2026-11-12T00:23:15.320Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round-6 final validation: eight scoped files pass, 109/109 reported tests across two suites, zero failures/skips/cancellations. This includes every static changed-script test importer, the shared proof subprocess consumer, workflow and shipped-document checks. Each file has a strict 1200-second cap and at most two active workers. After the fixture-only portable-PM resolver correction, repeated only the affected drift and clone/archive proof files: 29/29 pass; portability file 342.89 seconds, targeted rerun 386.10 seconds. Fresh single-branch clone and source archive both complete all 54 shared mutations/56 proof cases with 25 passing restored controls. Typecheck and test compilation pass on final text; docstrings pass (57 files, 289 declarations). Six boundary tests also passed through pm test --run --progress. Lifecycle stress is deliberately skipped locally for CI per round-6 instruction; no live Windows execution or full release coverage claim. No new CLI/SDK gap identified. Main is unchanged at 9b2c446 and already merged; accepted round-5 and native append-only history remain intact. Exact-head CI and remaining lifecycle certification are visible on https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/341/checks ."
  "2026-11-12T00:23:16.202Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final handoff: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CP fixes actual published gitHead/tag boundary selection, main ancestry and refusal diagnostics; full boundary revert fails 2 assertions. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CM validates frozen non-change disposition and symmetric status/time/declaration facts; full attribution revert fails 1 assertion and frozen implemented must-allow passes. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CT makes command validation and execution follow the reported shell/existing helper and uses the portable installed-PM resolver; reinstating the POSIX-only assertion or default interpreter fails its regression. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Z7CE documents only the actual file-check receipt categories; restoring old documentation fails its contract assertion. Four full threads, four complete comments and all four AI-agent prompt sections read. No thread replies, reactions or resolutions. Commit the code, docs, tests and native PM evidence together; release the own claim, keep this item in_progress, regenerate/check after all PM writes and push the existing PR. Working tree mutations for revert proofs occurred only in disposable copies."
  "2026-11-12T04:43:19.691Z",codex-agent,"Closing review: pulled accepted PR head d09e238, merged main 0620c50 via a standard merge while retaining #344 case-insensitive dependency matching and this PR rendering profiles; rebuilt generated maps instead of hand-merging them. No pending merge receipts; existing legacy health warnings remain unchanged. Read every unresolved thread with all comments and latest CodeRabbit review body: two unresolved threads (four comments), one outside-diff finding. Address only branch coverage, native timeout registration, historical empty-group compatibility and the remaining proof-determinism concern associated with the existing proof thread; preserve all thresholds and native histories. Use codex-agent for this closing round. No thread replies, resolutions, mentions or PR merge."
  "2026-11-12T04:51:34.341Z",codex-agent,"Closing fixes verified against the code: file-check diagnosis returns only rendering_changed/tracker_changed, so the old CLI reorder-only message alternative was unreachable. Removed that branch without changing thresholds or ignores and added genuine empty-tracker in-process historical-profile and missing-file receipts. Historical empty release/milestone group fallback now follows the published 2026.11.6 source, including version/date headings, empty claims and deliberate suppression; current output stays suppressed. Restored the cited native timeout_seconds=1200 and audited equivalent wrapper registrations: index 8 and three newer file registrations had the same omission and were corrected through pinned pm. Added a public SDK regression checking all declared wrapper/native budgets. Remaining old thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZe is valid: a movable merge base made the proof source change across runs. The proof now always mutates checked-out source, with a real Git regression moving origin/main while HEAD stays fixed. All four unresolved-thread comments and the full outside-diff AI prompt were read; no replies/resolutions. Post-merge generator/dependency/pending/drift tests passed 246/246."
  "2026-11-12T05:15:22.766Z",codex-agent,"Closing bounded coverage attempt: exact npm run coverage was capped at 1200 seconds and returned timeout 124. Node reported 919 passing tests, zero assertion failures and 18 cancellations from termination; the partial coverage report is not a full-suite verdict. The long proof/lifecycle workload did not finish on this host; no thresholds or presence checks changed. Full npm/Bun release certification remains with CI because repeating those suites would exceed the closing budget. Independent disposable regressions pass five controls, then restoring only createChangelog fails the historical empty-group test (1 assertion), restoring only the old proof baseline module fails the remote-main-advance invariant (1 assertion), and unsetting only the cited native timeout through pinned pm fails the registration test (1 assertion). All five controls pass again after restoration; native scratch history is append-only and the source worktree was never reverted. A separate strict CLI-source 100/100/100 coverage proof over all 16 in-process CLI importer files is running; it will also test reintroduction of the old unreachable branch and restored controls. Self-review covered category branches in CLI/extension, historical fallback headings/suppression, checked-out proof selection and all wrapper/native timeout pairs. No remaining linked proof lacks an explicit native timeout."
  "2026-11-12T06:00:57.075Z",codex-agent,"Closing coverage cause confirmed: the initial unreachable-message hypothesis was not causal. Strict controls on Node 26 pass 38/38 with the original accepted d09e238 CLI implementation and measure cli.ts at 100% lines/branches/functions. Removed only the new in-process missing-output-file check in an owned clone: all 38 behavioral tests still pass but the unchanged 100% branch gate rejects 99.70%; restoring that check restores 100/100/100. Preserved the accepted CLI source and its compiled output instead of shipping the unnecessary message edit. Additional real-tracker in-process controls cover JSON aliases, fallback dates, statuses, explicit dependency/link options, bounded diffs, structured refusal routing and error exits so the CLI-only coverage measurement is complete without unrelated slow randomized SDK models. No threshold, presence requirement or ignore changed. The closing fixes therefore remain test coverage, native timeout metadata, historical comparison fallback and deterministic proof input."
  "2026-11-12T06:20:58.528Z",codex-agent,"Closing final evidence: Node 26.13.0 and Node 22.23.4 each pass the 38 selected real/in-process CLI cases and measure all of cli.ts at 100% lines, branches and functions with unchanged 100% thresholds and no ignores. On Node 26, removing only the new missing-file check makes that strict gate reject 99.70%; restoring it restores 100/100/100 while retaining the accepted CLI implementation. Historical fallback, moving-ref determinism and timeout metadata each fail their independent reverted assertion, with five controls restored. The repaired exact native registration ran via pm test --run --match with progress and no --timeout override: passed in 145678 ms, beyond the old 120-second default, using its stored 1200-second budget. Its nine fixed/restored controls and all four empty-Unreleased mutations pass (14 expected assertion failures, six proof cases). Post-merge generator/dependency/pending/drift run: 246/246. Final CLI/registration/shipped-docs run: 18/18; direct Bun CLI/SDK smoke: 2/2 without git on PATH. Build, test compilation, typecheck, docstrings (57 files, 289 declarations), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), both pack checks and publish-attestation audit pass. No lint script exists. Self-host health passes the exact CI warning baseline in a clean HOME without ignored extension fixtures; the owned ignored fixture was restored in finally. Ambient global-extension notices are unchanged. Full npm coverage attempt was incomplete at its 20-minute cap (919 pass, zero assertion failures, 18 cancellations); full npm/Bun release certification remains with CI. No new SDK gap identified."
  "2026-11-12T06:20:59.420Z",codex-agent,"Closing handoff: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZe now uses checked-out proof source independently of mutable Git refs; regression advances origin/main while HEAD stays fixed. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62budF now stores timeout_seconds=1200 on the cited proof and equivalent declared wrappers; SDK registration regression and actual native run prove the budget. Latest CodeRabbit review 5867841443 outside-diff generator finding now retains historical release/milestone empty-group output, version/date headings, empty claims and deliberate suppression; current output remains unchanged. CI coverage gap is covered through the real missing-output-file in-process check, with 100/100/100 on both CI runtimes. Standard main merge 475413e preserves #344 dependency-subject matching and rendering profiles; main remains 0620c50. All two unresolved threads/four comments plus full review-body AI prompt read, and no replies or resolutions sent. Release only the own codex-agent claim, keep own item in_progress, regenerate/check after final writes, commit native PM evidence with the fixes and push the same PR. Exact-head CI remains at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/341/checks ."
  "2026-11-12T15:24:41.903Z",codex-agent,"Round 8: read all three unresolved CodeRabbit threads and complete AI prompts on f9251e5. Current main 3f66576 is already merged by d4598e4; fast-forwarded the review branch and installed its pinned dependencies. Fix unavailable-boundary refusal only with eligible candidates, prove absence through the full registry packument after an exact-version 404, and round-trip empty status lists through canonical regeneration guidance. Preserve per-item published-boundary skips and all 100-percent coverage thresholds. Add disposable mutants, run bounded targeted gates and coverage, then commit tracker evidence with code and release only this claim."
  "2026-11-12T15:26:43.001Z",codex-agent,"Round 8 implementation and six focused controls pass. Eligible delivered rendering items now cause an explicit reasoned refusal before writes when the release boundary is missing; no eligible candidate still succeeds, and published per-item skips remain intact. An exact-version 404 now requires a full application/json packument with valid time and versions maps, HTTP 200 and no version in either map before authorizing unpublished. Real local HTTP tests cover absent, error, malformed, time-only and versions-only evidence. Empty status arrays serialize as comma and round-trip alongside nonempty statuses. Expanded the existing disposable proof with five mutants for these fixes and the must-allow twin."
  "2026-11-12T15:36:50.482Z",codex-agent,"Round 8 complete disposable revert proof PASS: 61/61 proof cases, with 27 fixed controls and 27 restored controls. Each new mutant causes an assertion failure: skip-missing-release-boundary, refuse-without-release-candidates, trust-exact-version-404, accept-packument-without-time, and empty-status-guidance. The first proof attempt correctly rejected the must-allow mutation but reported a raw rejected promise; wrapped that success control in assert.doesNotReject and reran every mutation successfully. No production-source mutation touched the review checkout. Existing unproved-publication assertions in the boundary test now require the same reasoned refusal; known-boundary skips and the published/unpublished must-allow tests remain. Native 21-file importer/CLI/coverage gate is still running; full coverage follows within its independent 20-minute cap."
  "2026-11-12T15:46:24.504Z",codex-agent,"Round 8 native PM-linked gate PASS: 255/255 tests in 21 files, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 851.108 seconds of tests and 858.853 seconds recorded native execution. It covers every direct test importer of cli.ts and both changed attribution/boundary modules, plus CLI regressions, file-diff and PM registration tests. All of src/cli.ts measures 100 percent lines, branches and functions at the unchanged strict thresholds. The native run used its stored 1200-second budget with progress. Typecheck, test compilation and docstrings pass; no lint script exists. Starting the exact repository npm run coverage command with a separate 1200-second cap; full npm/Bun release certification remains separate CI evidence if that cap is reached."
  "2026-11-12T16:07:25.938Z",codex-agent,"Round 8 exact npm run coverage attempt reached its independent 1200-second cap and exited 124. It emitted no final test-count or coverage verdict; no ERR_ASSERTION marker appeared before termination. Do not treat its partial results or killed file workers as a completed coverage certificate. The completed 255/255 native importer gate measures all of cli.ts at 100/100/100. Full repository npm/Bun release certification remains with CI under the host budget. Updated the previously registered focused CLI coverage command to include the new empty-status test, preserving its native 1200-second budget; now running that focused gate on Node 22 as the second CI runtime."
  "2026-11-12T16:09:02.618Z",codex-agent,"Round 8 final handoff: all three CodeRabbit threads and three complete comments/AI prompts read. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62mMEQ refuses unavailable attribution boundaries with eligible delivered items before any writes; no eligible items still succeed and known published boundaries retain per-item skips. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62mMEa requires HTTP 200 full application/json packument evidence with valid time/versions maps absent the version; all uncertain and malformed cases remain unknown. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62mMEg preserves empty status lists as comma and round-trips parsed regeneration options with a nonempty twin. Native Node 26 importer gate: 255/255 in 21 files, 100/100/100 for all of cli.ts. Native Node 22 focused gate: 39/39, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100/100/100 for all of cli.ts, recorded in 112179 ms. Full disposable proof: 61/61 cases, 27 fixed and 27 restored controls, 61 expected mutation assertion failures, including all five new mutants. Build, typecheck, test compilation and docstring gate pass; no lint script exists. Exact npm coverage reached its 20-minute cap without a complete verdict or assertion marker; full npm/Bun certification remains CI responsibility at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/341/checks . No thresholds or ignores changed. Native histories preserve main prefixes and added-line privacy scans pass after execution receipts. Main remains 3f66576, already present in f9251e5. Release only this codex-agent claim, keep this item in_progress, then run final clean-home health and changelog regeneration/check, commit the tracker with code and rebuilt dist, and push. No review replies/resolutions or new SDK gap."
  "2026-11-12T19:40:16.330Z",steve-orchestrator,"Orchestrator fixes for CodeRabbit review of 7c56829: (1) readPublicationState proves absence only from a packument whose top-level name is the requested package; a missing or different name is unknown. Absence fixtures carry the name; missing-name and other-package cases expect unknown (fail on revert). (2) New test: an annotated v2.0.0 tag resolves to the published commit, not the tag object (fails when the ^{commit} peel is removed); its must-refuse twin, an annotated tag peeling to a tree, resolves to no boundary with one reason. (3) docs/release.md: with eligible items, unknown publication or missing Git evidence logs each candidate and fails the release step before any write; with no eligible items the release continues. Gate: rendering-release-boundary and release-rendering-attribution tests (14 pass), tsc, changelog:check."
  "2026-11-12T21:05:49.545Z",orchestrator,"Orchestrator, CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOSfkApc620e1b and Greptile PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62zkzD on 49aeb72. (1) The default test run no longer runs the complete mutation proof twice. test/proof-baseline.test.ts runs scripts/prove-check-generator-drift-revert.ts --baseline-only in the fresh clone and in the source archive. ProofRun case selection runs only fixed-controls and restored-controls there, and the full proof stays the registered pm test. (2) The packument map fixtures now carry name=fixture, so the time and versions guards are what refuse them. With the time guards removed, release-rendering-attribution fails 1 of 7. Gates: proof-run, release-rendering-attribution and proof-baseline pass 13/13 (168 s, was 343 s+ for the proof alone)."
  "2026-11-12T21:46:16.486Z",orchestrator,"Orchestrator, round 9 review fixes on d0c3a40: Greptile PRRT_kwDOSfkApc621RCs, CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOSfkApc622AmS and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc622Amg. (1) canonicalRegenerationOptions maps the accepted plural exclude-tags/excludeTags aliases to exclude-tag, with the native precedence (registered spelling, then camelCase, then alias), so the regeneration command keeps the caller's exclusions. (2) Rendering attribution compares completions at the release commit's whole-second resolution: a completion inside that second is attributed, and the next second is not. (3) Without gitHead the boundary accepts v<version> or <version> tags, and refuses published_tag_ambiguous when both exist and disagree. test/release-boundary-round9.test.ts fails 3 of 3 with the source reverted. Gates: the round 9, attribution and generator-drift files pass 37/37; build, typecheck, docstring and changelog:check pass."
